{"qid":"Q241","names":["Republic of Cuba","Communist Cuba"],"title":"Republic of Cuba","endonym":{"native":"República de Cuba","lang":"es"},"capsule":"The Republic of Cuba was established on 20 May 1902 after U.S. military occupation following the Spanish-American War, but sovereignty was constrained by the Platt Amendment (1901), which authorized American intervention and guaranteed the Guantánamo naval base lease. The period encompassed two U.S. military interventions (1906–1909, 1917–1922), the Machado dictatorship (1925–1933), and Batista's return to power via coup in 1952. Fidel Castro's guerrilla campaign ended on 1 January 1959 when Batista fled; the revolutionary government nationalized U.S. properties and aligned with the Soviet Union, prompting the trade embargo beginning in 1960 that marked the effective end of the prior republican order.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Cuban national territory is precisely defined as an island state; the dataset period 1905–1960 captures the pre-revolutionary republic with unambiguous boundaries.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Cuba","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Cuba"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Cuba","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuba"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Platt Amendment","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platt_Amendment"}],"britannica":"place/Cuba","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Cuba","rulers":[{"qid":"Q5042604","name":"Carlos Saladrigas Zayas","start":1940,"end":1942,"image":"Carlos saladrigas.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Carlos%20saladrigas.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Pu